<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕceptrix</span></b> ,
		īcis, f.
		receptor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>She that receives</i>, <i><span class="en">App.
				Mund. p. 66, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Asclep. p.
				77, 30</span></i>; p. 287 Bip.; <i><span class="en">Ambros. in
				Luc. 8, 52</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In a bad sense, <i>she that harbors</i> or
				<i>conceals</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Messana, praedarum ac furtorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 8, § 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 5, 62, § 160</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
